# Written at INSTALL time (cmake/install_pc.cmake), in one of two flavours,
# because only the install knows its prefix:
#
#  * a system prefix (/usr, the .deb/.rpm): the prefix is that literal path,
#    so pkg-config recognises -I/usr/include and the system -L as system
#    directories and drops them (doppler#1547), and there is no rpath -- the
#    packages register the library with ldconfig.
#  * anything else (the release tarball, `jbx get-doppler`, ~/.local):
#    RELOCATABLE. The prefix is derived from this file's own location
#    (<prefix>/<libdir>/pkgconfig/doppler.pc), so an extracted tree works
#    wherever it lands -- not only the build-time CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX -- and
#    Libs carries an rpath (below). The hop count back to the prefix is DERIVED
#    from the libdir (DOPPLER_PC_TO_PREFIX in CMakeLists.txt): it was a literal
#    `../..`, right for lib/ and lib64/ and wrong for Debian's
#    lib/<multiarch>/, where it resolved the prefix to /usr/lib.
prefix=@DOPPLER_PC_PREFIX@
exec_prefix=${prefix}
libdir=${exec_prefix}/@DOPPLER_PC_LIBDIR@
includedir=${prefix}/@DOPPLER_PC_INCLUDEDIR@

Name: doppler
Description: doppler C library
Version: @DOPPLER_PC_VERSION@
# -lm and -lpthread are in Libs, NOT Libs.private, and that is deliberate
# (doppler#1450). Private is for what only libdoppler itself calls. doppler's
# headers define code -- every step() is inline, dp_thread.h and the ring are
# header-only -- so libm and pthread symbols are undefined in the CONSUMER's
# object, and a shared link does not resolve those through libdoppler.so's own
# NEEDED entries. With them private, `cc main.c $(pkg-config --cflags --libs
# doppler)` failed on an inline agc_step() everywhere, and on dp_thread.h
# wherever glibc < 2.34 keeps pthread in its own library. The same two serve
# the static link, so there is nothing left to list as private.
#
# The optional NATS stream layer has its own module: `pkg-config --cflags
# --libs doppler_stream` gives the complete streaming link line (it Requires:
# this core module, and inherits these through it).
#
# The rpath flag in Libs: present in the relocatable flavour, absent for a
# system prefix and on Windows (cmake/install_pc.cmake). A .pc that names -L
# but not an rpath builds a binary that links and then cannot RUN unless the
# prefix is on the loader path, which an extracted release tarball
# (`jbx get-doppler`, ~/.local/doppler) never is. The exported CMake target
# records its library directory for the build tree; this is the same promise
# for the other consumer, and stream inherits it through Requires.
Libs: -L${libdir}@DOPPLER_PC_RPATH@ -ldoppler -lm -lpthread
# The feature-test macro is part of the contract, not a convenience: the
# installed headers call syscall()/ftruncate() and name MAP_ANONYMOUS, which a
# strict -std=c99 hides on glibc < 2.34 unless it is defined BEFORE libc is
# first reached -- so it has to be on the compile line, and only this file can
# put it there for a pkg-config consumer (doppler#1451). Substituted from the
# one declaration the build and the exported CMake target also read.
Cflags: -I${includedir}@DOPPLER_PC_FEATURE_CFLAGS@
